Hygon Information Technology Co., Ltd. has modified the NVIDIA PhysX
sources to add Hygon HCU (HIP) support. The changes cover new HIP runtime,
kernel and build files, edits to GPU kernel sources, and the CPU/GPU build
scripts. Original NVIDIA source files keep their upstream copyright and
license notices unchanged; the Hygon contributions are distributed under
the same BSD-3-Clause terms as the upstream project.

## Hygon modification register

The following upstream files contain substantive Hygon compatibility or
implementation changes. Their original NVIDIA, AGEIA, and NovodeX notices
are retained unchanged; the Hygon contributions are registered here at the
repository level under BSD-3-Clause, as required for modified upstream
files:

- `physx/source/gpucommon/include/PxgCommonDefines.h`: HIP-aware warp
  definitions and compatibility includes.
- `physx/source/gpunarrowphase/include/PxgNpKernelIndices.h`: HCU/HIP
  kernel launch-index adjustments.
- `physx/source/gpunarrowphase/src/CUDA/cudaSphere.cu`: HIP-compatible
  sphere narrow-phase guarding and bounds handling.
- `physx/source/gpunarrowphase/src/CUDA/warpHelpers.cuh`: generalized
  warp/wavefront reduction helpers.
- `physx/source/gpucommon/src/CUDA/shuffle.cuh`: explicit warp-width
  shuffles for HIP.

The remaining modified upstream source files contain non-substantive
portability edits such as HIP include guards, CUDA-to-HIP type mappings,
platform conditionals, and whitespace normalization. Those files also keep
their original notices unchanged and do not carry a separate Hygon
copyright line.

Files created by Hygon carry a Hygon copyright notice, the SPDX identifier
`BSD-3-Clause`, and the complete BSD-3-Clause text. Repository metadata and
third-party notices are not source files and therefore do not carry an
additional SPDX source header.

Third-party components carried by this repository are listed in
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
